    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Charming circa 1935 detached three-bedroom bungalow, nestled on a beautifully mature approx 0.5-acre site with a selection of block-built sheds, in the heart of town, this charming bungalow presents a rare opportunity to acquire a home of character, space and outstanding potential. Set in a cul de sac position amidst established gardens, the property enjoys a peaceful and private setting while remaining just a short stroll from all amenities both social and essential that Castlepollard has to offer including a selection of local shops, pubs, Hotel, coffee shop, Church's, Tesco shopping centre, Gym, two primary schools and a post primary school. Serviced with the New TFI Local Link 818 Mullingar to Castlepollard via Collinstown, offering 5 daily return services Monday to Thursday, 8 on Friday, 7 on Saturday and 5 on Sundays and within easy access of many lakes and rivers for water sport and fishing enthusiasts, Tullynally Castle garden and forestry walks on your door step. Lough Lene Blue Flag Lake in Collinstown is less than a 10-minute drive famed for fishing, swimming and water sports.\n\nThe accommodation comprises of a welcoming entrance porch leading to the living room with front aspect, solid fuel fireplace and timber flooring. Three well-proportioned bedrooms, a fully tiled family bathroom and fully fitted kitchen to the rear with tiled flooring and solid fuel range.\n\nThe home retains much of its original charm, while comfortable as it stands, it also provides an excellent opportunity for modernisation or extension (subject to the necessary planning permissions).\n\nOutside, the magnificent half-acre site is a standout feature with mature trees, established hedging and expansive lawns create a lovely private space rarely\nfound within a town centre location. The generous grounds offer endless possibilities for gardening enthusiasts, outdoor entertaining or future development.\n\nProperties of this nature seldom come to the market, this is an ideal opportunity for families, downsizers, or those seeking a unique property with enormous potential.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Porch 1.445m x 1.844m (4'9\" x 6'1\"):\nPVC door and window, tiled flooring, radiator.\n\nSitting Room 4.300m x 4.400m (14'1\" x 14'5\"):\nFront aspect, laminate flooring, coving, solid fuel fireplace with timber surround.\n\nBedroom One 2.237m x 4.608m (7'4\" x 15'1\"):\nOff the sitting room, front aspect, carpet flooring, coving.\n\nBedroom Two 4.674m x 2.170m (15'4\" x 7'1\"):\nDouble room, off sitting room, front aspect, carpet flooring, coving, stira to attic.\n\nInner Hall 0.960m x 6.660m (3'2\" x 21'10\"):\nPVC door to side entrance, coving, tiled flooring, dado rail.\n\nKitchen 4.240m x 3.552m (13'11\" x 11'8\"):\nDual aspect side and rear, fitted timber units, tiled flooring, tiled splashback, coving, solid fuel range, hot-press shelved with immersion.\n\nBedroom Three 4.686m x 2.521m (15'4\" x 8'3\"):\nDouble room with rear aspect, carpet flooring, two sets of fitted wardrobes, coving.\n\nBathroom 3.549m x 2.214m (11'8\" x 7'3\"):\nFully tiled, contains WC, wash hand basin, bath with shower, shower screen, built in storage.\n\nOutbuildings\nShed One 3.354m x 5.120m (11' x 16'10\"):\nBlock built, concrete base, power supply\n\nShed Two 5.120m x 2.789m (16'10\" x 9'2\"):\nBlock built, concrete base\n\nShed Three 5.321m x 1.870m (17'5\" x 6'2\"):\nPlumbed, power supply, currently being used for laundry room.\n\nShed Four 5.321m x 3.931m (17'5\" x 12'11\"):\nConcrete base, up and over door, power point\n\nShed Five 5.316m x 4.247m (17'5\" x 13'11\"):\nConcrete base, power supply\n\nIncluded in Sale\nCurtains\nBlinds\nLight fittings\nGas cooker\nFridge\nWashing machine\nFixtures & Fittings\n\nFeatures & Services\nBuilt c.1935\nAppox 94.44 sq.m\nThree spacious bedrooms\nMature 0.5-acre approx site\nBeautiful established gardens\nPrivate and peaceful setting\nExcellent opportunity to modernise or extend (SPP)\nWalking distance to town centre\nWalking distance to Post primary school\nPVC facia & soffits\nDouble glazed window and doors\nOutside tap\nAmple parking space\n\nBER Details\nBER Rating: G\nBER No. 119663185\n\nDirections\nFrom Castlepollard town centre proceed out Water Street passing the primary school on the right and take the cul de sac to the\nright the house is located on the left-hand side. Eircode N91 HT38"
